  "source_review": {
    "definition": "Maximize edge count of an induced path in Q_d. Keep d=9 and add10/11. No repeated vertices or nonconsecutive cube neighbors. Coils and snakepits are different objectives.",
    "primary_source": "Sol read Orland et al. arXiv2607.15270v3 Table1, exact optima known through dimension8, current paper constructions379 and746. The table footnote credits later750 to Echols2026a; it remains reported only in this archive. Paper discloses LLM assistance for search code. No global optimality proof for10/11 was found in checked sources.",
    "witness_reconstruction": "Sol fetched record_snakes.csv.zip at authors commit46c765399353a588ea50444a5d6610f53102b1c2, size16721566, Git blob SHA1 7854e2592325dab85a35a8a4809314edb80f7af8. Extracted the matching rows and verified every transition against saved vertices. Certified scores379 and746.",
    "human_method": "Wynn2012 190-edge Q9 path extended into Q10/Q11 by one endpoint move per new coordinate, giving191/192. In each added coordinate layer only the new endpoint is used, with exactly one neighbor in the preceding layer. This is a verified historical-method reconstruction and is weaker than the public record.",
    "independent_method": "Sol ran human and reference. Separate neighbor-set enumeration over all d coordinate flips verifies precisely the path edges. Check crossing count (d-2)m+2 <= d*(2^d-m), giving upper bounds567/1125 edges. Complete score-claim invariance, bad vertices, strict replay, cold isolated generation and failure controls passed.",
    "admission": "Five valid strict programs for all3 configs. Preserve original Q9 archives. Q11 formal public reference746; report750 remains separate."
  }
